      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $6$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}24+(2z-5)\\cdot 6 & = \\\\ 24+2z\\cdot 6+(-5)\\cdot 6 & = \\\\ 24+(12z)+(-30) & = \\\\ 24+12z-30\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24+12z-30 & = \\\\ 12z+(24-30) & = \\\\ 12\\,z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
